1. DEFINITIONS
   "the Work" means the game Debt Master: its source code, its text, its game
   design and balance data, its visual design, and its name.
   "the Author" means Guillaume Brin.

2. WHAT YOU MAY DO, FREELY AND WITHOUT ASKING
   a) Play the Work, at the official address or from a local copy.
   b) Read, study and learn from the source code, including for teaching.
   c) Keep a private copy on your own machine for your own use.
   d) Link to the official address, write about the Work, review it, stream it,
      record it, and show it to other people.

3. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO WITHOUT THE AUTHOR'S PRIOR WRITTEN PERMISSION
   a) Redistribute the Work or any substantial part of it — this includes
      hosting it at another address, republishing it, packaging it as an
      application, or bundling it with anything else.
   b) Publish a modified version, a translation, a port, or a derivative work.
   c) Use the Work, or any part of it, commercially. This includes selling it,
      hosting it alongside advertising, using it to promote a product, or
      including it in any paid offering.
   d) Remove, obscure or alter the copyright notices in the source.
   e) Use the name "Debt Master", or a name confusingly similar to it, for a
      game or an interactive work.

4. RESERVATION OF TEXT AND DATA MINING RIGHTS
   The Author expressly reserves the rights of reproduction and extraction for
   the purposes of text and data mining, including for the training of machine
   learning or generative models, within the meaning of Article 4(3) of
   Directive (EU) 2019/790 and of Article L.122-5-3 of the French Intellectual
   Property Code. No such use is permitted without prior written agreement.

5. PERMISSIONS
   Permission for anything in section 3 may be granted, and is often granted
   for non-commercial and educational projects. Ask.

6. NO WARRANTY
   The Work is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or
   implied. The Author is not liable for any claim, damage or other liability
   arising from the Work or its use.

7. GOVERNING LAW
   This licence is governed by French law. In case of any divergence between
   the English and French versions below, the French version prevails.

